  play ssh/pve9 ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: ssh/pve9$
# web-01.example.net is a Proxmox VE 9 node as installed:$
# PermitRootLogin yes, passwords on; root alone, by key; no ufw.$
# hardn runs from root's login.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [ ] SSH Login            Not Configured root allowed$
  [ ] SSH Auth             Not Configured password auth on$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured default (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Root SSH Login       Allowed by sshd_config$
  [ ] Password Login       On sshd's default$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         root, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Root key-only        Kept for the Proxmox VE cluster$
   2) Key-only login       Turn password login off$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 1$
$
# Root key-only ################################################$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      @@ -0,0 +1,23 @@$
      +# hardn's boot unit (P-34 (c);$
      | docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs$
      +# it before it arms the revert timer of a change that$
      | could lock you out, and$
      +# removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.$
      +#$
      +# At boot, before sshd reads its files: re-arm the revert$
      | timer of a change$
      +# waiting for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its$
      | window, or roll the$
      +# change back when its deadline has passed. Ordering$
      | only: sshd starts$
      +# whatever this unit does.$
      +[Unit]$
      +Description=hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an$
      | unconfirmed change$
      +DefaultDependencies=no$
      +After=local-fs.target sysinit.target ufw.service$
      +Before=ssh.service ssh.socket sshd.service sshd.socket$
      | shutdown.target$
      +Conflicts=shutdown.target$
      +$
      +[Service]$
      +Type=oneshot$
      +RemainAfterExit=yes$
      +ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot$
      +TimeoutStartSec=7min$
      +$
      +[Install]$
      +WantedBy=multi-user.target$
      -not installed$
      +installed and enabled$
      $ systemd-analyze verify --recursive-errors=no$
      | /run/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Disallow root password login$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn.$
      +# Set by hardn:$
      +PermitRootLogin prohibit-password$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
$
      ssh.service$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      sshd -T shows no root password login$
$
      sshd -T$
      $ sshd -T$
$
  Make root key-only?$
$
  Type the hostname [web-01, 0 or q]: web-01$
$
  [+] Install hardn's boot unit             Done$
  [+] Disallow root password login          Done$
  [+] Reload sshd (ssh.service)             Done$
  [+] sshd -T shows no root password login  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 3:01$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session and run:$
$
      $ hardn confirm$
$
  Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx is rolled$
  back at 12:03:01 UTC. To undo it now, run hardn rollback$
  20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root key-only (Proxmox)$
  [ ] SSH Auth             Not Configured password auth on$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured default (22)$
$
  SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Key only$
  [ ] Password Login       On sshd's default$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         root, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Root key-only        Kept for the Proxmox VE cluster$
   2) Key-only login       Turn password login off$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: ssh/pve9$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/systemd/system/hardn-boot.service$
      $ systemctl --no-reload enable hardn-boot.service$
$
   -  Armed the revert timer$
      $ systemd-run$
      | --unit=hardn-revert-20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
      | "--description=hardn: roll back change$
      | 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx unless confirmed"$
      | --on-active=180s --timer-property=AccuracySec=1s$
      | /usr/local/bin/hardn rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
   -  Applied: Disallow root password login$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
$
   -  Applied: Reload sshd (ssh.service)$
      $ systemctl reload ssh.service$
$

